    </dependency>



    <!-- Guava: siddhi-core 5.1.2 shaded guava 23; 5.1.33 pulls guava 33.0.0-jre transitively.
         Every consumer bundle (controller/wsapi/stunnel) was compiled against the old export
         and imports com.google.common.* with range [23,24). siddhi 5.1.33's own OSGi range is
         [23,34), so pinning guava to 23.x satisfies BOTH — the library keeps exporting a 23.x
         version, no consumer needs rebuilding, and there is zero guava API drift (this is the
         exact guava line the whole system was already built and tested on). -->
